    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d951">

                <pb facs="0888" n="784" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg784"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6944.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-30T13:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 30, 1913—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>145. The necessity for an immediate meeting for the consideration of recognition
                    and of general claims is urged on me by my diplomatic colleagues, but as I have
                    no instructions as to recognition I declined to call a meeting at the Embassy
                    and said I would participate in one at the British Legation. Please send
                    instruction at once.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
